         "step": 1,
         "text": "The outermost operation is a product of \\( 4 x^{3} \\) and \\( e^{2 x + 2} \\), so the product rule comes first; the second factor is a composite, so its derivative needs the chain rule with inner function \\( 2 x + 2 \\).",
         "rule_named": "classify the outermost operation"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "So \\( h'(x) = 8 x^{3} e^{2 x + 2} + 12 x^{2} e^{2 x + 2} \\).",
         "rule_named": "product rule, then chain rule"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "At x = 1 the exponent is 4 and its derivative is 2, so \\( h'(1) = 20 e^{4} \\).",
